Found under k350 (apply worker, 2026-10-31). OCP::Drift's probes for NFD (DaemonSet node-feature-discovery/nfd-worker) and the GPU Operator (Deployment gpu-operator/gpu-operator) are self_healing: ocp status counts an image changed in the cluster (kubectl set image, an edit) as drift that `ocp apply` closes. But setup_nfd and setup_gpu_operator in lib/OCP/Cmd/Apply/Workloads.pm only compare the recorded options hash in .ocp/deployed.yaml and check presence. So the real run says up to date, deploys nothing, and the drift stays; the dry run says the same. That is the shape k350 fixed for the four AMD GPU DaemonSets.

Fix as k350 did: read the object the way the probe does, through OCP::Drift->version_against_pin (added in k350). On an off-pin tag, redeploy and report "ran X, expected Y"; the dry run says "runs X, expected Y / would update it". If a redeploy cannot restore the pinned image for one of them, mark that probe report-only instead, and say why.

Lane: ocp-apply-worker. Needs k350 committed (version_against_pin).

Done = for a changed image on both NFD and the GPU Operator, ocp status, the dry run and the real run agree, covered by tests shaped like t/251's k350 subtests: red first, then a mutation check.

